ing and no visible outside support. Bynum is already on the air with her first TV ad and has no outside groups opposing her.\n\nAll nine expert raters place the race in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and prediction markets price Bynum's chances at 93 to 95 percent. No general-election polls are available, so the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and money, all of which point to a comfortable incumbent win in a year when Oregon's districts are widely viewed as safe.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9797, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 15.3}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9806, "margin": 15.0}]}